  "summary": "Power steering (N40) pump installation at the front of the engine: the pump is bolted to a front bracket and a mounting assembly screwed to the engine, braced by a rear support, with nuts on its own studs. The pump pulley is held by a nut and driven by a belt from the crankshaft pulley; a guard is bolted to the pump rear. The pressure hose screws into the pump and the return (inlet) hose is clamped; both hoses are clipped together and run to the steering control valve (sheet A4).",
